# The Piper J-3 Cub's checklists: this project's own words, following the
# aeroplane's own Owner's Manual.
#
# **The source is Piper's Owner's Manual for the J3C-65**, the same manual
# docs/ASSETS.md records for this aircraft's figures, read for its "Flying
# Hints", pages 37 to 42 - sections A to H: before starting the engine,
# starting, warm-up, stopping, taxiing, general flying, approach and landing,
# and parking. The copy read is the one ASSETS.md names, at
# <https://stpeteair.org/wp-content/uploads/cub_owners_manual.pdf>.
#
# **It carries no text layer, and did not need one.** The item this file
# belongs to had recorded the Cub as unsourceable because both copies are
# scans; the pages were read as pages.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# The Cub has no flaps at all, so nothing here names one. Its undercarriage is
# fixed and it sits on a tailwheel, and its propeller is fixed-pitch, so there
# is no gear lever and no pitch lever either. Nor is there an electrical
# system: no starter, no lights, and a wire float on the tank cap for a fuel
# gauge. Its panel is a throttle and a carburettor heat control, with no
# mixture lever to set, so those items are the pilot's to confirm.
#
# The stick back is a negative elevator command, which is why the two items
# that ask for it read as they do.
#
# **The manual is in miles an hour and the simulation reads knots**, so every
# speed below is converted and both are given: airborne at 39 m.p.h. is 34
# knots, best climb at 55 m.p.h. is 48, the cruise at 73 m.p.h. is 63, the
# glide at 50 to 60 m.p.h. is 43 to 52, and the 122 m.p.h. never-dive is 106.
# Each band is opened a little at each end, as the Cessnas' are, because the
# simulation reads calibrated and the manual is indicated.

phase before-start
# Sections A and B.
confirm Fuel checked on the wire float at the tank cap, twelve gallons full
confirm Oil checked to the four-quart mark, and the controls free
confirm Chocks in, brakes on, and someone who knows the controls in the cabin
confirm Ignition switch off and verified before the propeller is touched
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.15 Throttle set about a tenth open, section B
confirm Fuel shut-off on, contact called, and the propeller swung by hand

phase taxi
# Section C, warm-up, and section E, taxiing.
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 500.0 800.0 Idling at 700, and 550 to 600 once warm, section C
check fcs/elevator-cmd-norm <= -0.40 Stick held back taxiing upwind, section E
confirm Oil pressure up within thirty seconds, and no more than 220 degrees
confirm Magnetos checked at 2,100 with no more than 75 r.p.m. dropped, section C
confirm Weave the nose left and right, for nothing is visible straight ahead
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Taxi at the speed of a fast walk, section E

phase take-off
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Trim set for take-off
confirm Harness tight, controls free and correct, and the strip clear both ways
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Full throttle, headed into wind, section F
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 1950.0 Turning up towards the 2,300 take-off r.p.m., section F
confirm Tail lifted to the flying attitude as she gathers speed
check velocities/vc-kts >= 33.0 She flies herself off at about 39 m.p.h., 34 knots, section F

phase climb
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Throttle wide open, and not held there above three minutes, section F
range velocities/vc-kts 43.0 55.0 Best climb at 55 m.p.h., 48 knots, section F
check position/h-agl-ft >= 300.0 Three hundred feet before the first turn
confirm The nose lowered every few hundred feet to look ahead
confirm Oil pressure steady and above thirty pounds, section C

phase cruise
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 1950.0 2250.0 Cruising at 2,150 r.p.m., section F
range velocities/vc-kts 55.0 72.0 Which gives 73 m.p.h., 63 knots, section F
confirm Carburettor heat used if the engine runs rough, and off once it is clear, section F
confirm Altimeter set, and the fuel float watched as it sinks
confirm Nothing above 122 m.p.h., 106 knots, which is the diving limit, section F

phase descent
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.10 0.60 Throttle back for the descent
range velocities/vc-kts 43.0 60.0 Gliding between 50 and 60 m.p.h., 43 to 52 knots, section G
confirm Carburettor heat on before the throttle is closed, section G
confirm The engine cleared gently every 200 to 250 feet of a long glide, section G
confirm Altimeter set to the field's pressure

phase approach
range velocities/vc-kts 42.0 55.0 Holding the glide, 50 to 60 m.p.h., section G
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.50 Power well back on the approach
confirm Carburettor heat on, and the strip and its windsock in sight
confirm Sideslip off the height if she is high, for there are no flaps to help
confirm The approach flown in a gentle curve so the strip stays in view

phase landing
range velocities/vc-kts 32.0 45.0 Over the hedge at the bottom of the glide, slowing to the stall
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.20 Throttle closed in the round-out
check fcs/elevator-cmd-norm <= -0.70 Stick coming fully back as she settles
confirm Three-pointed, or wheeled on if the wind is strong
confirm Held straight with the rudder as she slows

phase after-landing
# Sections D and H.
check velocities/vc-kts <= 25.0 Clear of the strip and slowed to a taxi
check fcs/elevator-cmd-norm <= -0.40 Stick back again for the taxi
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttle back to a taxi power
confirm Carburettor heat off while idling, section D
confirm The engine idled some minutes before the switch is cut, section D
confirm Chocks in, ignition and fuel off, and the controls locked with the front belt, section H
